    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a defective DBR bandpass filter on Fused Silica substrate with Air incident medium. Structure: 25 finite layers total. Layer sequence from incident to substrate: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, SiO2 (defect), Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2. Initialize all Ta2O5 and SiO2 mirror layers to quarter-wave optical thickness at 1550 nm (physical thickness = 1550 / (4 * refractive_index)). Initialize the 13th layer (defect cavity, SiO2) to half-wave optical thickness at 1550 nm (physical thickness = 1550 / (2 * refractive_index)). Use Ta2O5 and SiO2 material registry entries. Optimize all 25 layer thicknesses to maximize transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Total layer count must remain exactly 25. Angle of incidence: 0 degrees (normal incidence). Polarization: unpolarized or both TE and TE evaluated. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
